WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.960
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim (LAM RIM),
Steps of the Path to Enlightenment.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.560
We were talking about nirvana.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.960
How to reach nirvana.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.040
What would it look like if I achieve nirvana?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:30.240
I always like to tell my friends how I grew up with four brothers and we were always fighting.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:37.880
And my little brother, two brothers under me,
he'd love to get me upset.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:45.240
He tried so hard to get me upset and I was famous in the family because no one can get me upset.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.000
But this brother could get me upset.
And if he gets me upset, he's so happy.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.840
"Ha! Ha! Ha! I got you upset!"

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.240
And he would do strange things.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:02.080
So if I reach nirvana nobody can get me upset, ever. Nobody. Not even my husband or wife.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.200
Nobody can make me upset.
Then you know you have reached nirvana.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.120
So that's nirvana.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.800
So we were talking about reaching nirvana,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:16.640
and we were talking about three trainings that help you get there. One is being nice to other people. Morality.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.560
What is the second one?
Meditation.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.360
And then the third one is understanding the pen, understanding emptiness.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.640
Now we reached a part about the teachings,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.560
and we talked about how being nice to other people is like the foundation of the teachings.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:44.560
If someone in a city is being nice to other people
then Buddhism exists there.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:50.680
Even if they don't believe in Buddhism, it doesn't matter.
Now he says, he's continuing,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.600
tenpa dzin shepa chu triy teng ne chu shepa chikpu la mi serwar
(BSTAN PA 'DZIN ZHES PA CHOS KHRI'I STENG NAS CHOS BSHAD PA GCIG PU LA MI ZER BAR)

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.720
We have this expression
in Buddhism called "Dharma Lord."
Like, "I'm a Dharma Master."

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.080
Okay, you can say Dharma Master.
So who's a Dharma Master?

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:13.800
What's a Dharma Master?
Some people say, "Oh, geshe, he translates.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.360
Dharma Master. You must be a Dharma Master.
You are a geshe." And he says, "Listen..."

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:28.480
He says here, "Dharma Master doesn't mean a geshe sitting on the teaching place and teaching Buddhism."

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.200
He says, "That's not a Dharma Master."

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.840
Then somebody said to him,
"What is a Dharma Master?"

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.040
He says, "A person who keeps the vows in their own heart.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.280
That's a Dharma Master."

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:51.880
Then they are a holder of the lineage.
They are a Dharma Lord. They are a Dharma Master.
They are holding the lineage of the Buddha.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:59.840
They are keeping the tradition of Buddhism in the world if they're being nice to other people.
That's a Dharma Master.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:09.840
I thought it's my job to find photographs, images that remind us of each point and

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.960
I found this image, and it's a lady,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.840
and she's sitting in her... I don't know... in her bedroom?

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.040
Guess what she's doing.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.440
She's preparing her taxes for this year.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.560
It's a very stressful time in every country, I think so.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:36.000
And the government expects you to finish the paperwork and prepare your taxes.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.200
So, this is a Dharma Master.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:44.120
I chose a picture of a Dharma Master.
This is a Dharma Master.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:52.000
This lady is a Dharma Master
and she's the real Dharma Master.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:04:00.160
She doesn't have this geshe hat, and she doesn't have beads on her arms, and she's not ringing a bell.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.320
But she's a Dharma Master. Why? Why?

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:13.840
She's keeping her vows. Okay?
Why? She's paying her taxes!
hundred percent of her taxes.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:18.000
If you want to be a really cool Dharma person,
if you want to be Dharma hip,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.800
then pay a hundred and five percent of your taxes,
or pay a hundred and eight percent of your taxes.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.280
@Zakat--automatic donation for the poor.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:33.720
Okay, pay extra taxes.
She's a Dharma Holder.
She's a Dharma Master.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.640
Why? She's paying her taxes on time.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.680
Because they help everybody in the country.
So she's a real Dharma Master.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:47.160
She's not teaching Buddhism on top of a throne with a big yellow hat and all these bells and things.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:53.480
She's a real Dharma Master. And it's not meant metaphorically; it's meant literally.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.840
She's a real Dharma Master.
So you want a Dharma Master?
Go look for somebody like that, okay?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.960
Next sentence:
lung chu la tu sam che na lung gi tenpa dzinpa dang--
(LUNG CHOS LA THOS BSAM BYAS NA
LUNG GI BSTAN PA 'DZIN PA DANG,)

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:18.040
If you study the written records of Buddhism,
if you go to the ACIP organization under John Brady,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:24.560
and you study the millions of pages
they have preserved in the world,

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:32.280
then, okay, we can call you a
Dharma Master of the written Dharma,
of the physical Dharma.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:37.920
We can call you a Dharma Master
of the physical Dharma.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:43.080
ke langpay tsultrim nam dak sung na tokpay tenpa dzinpa yin--
(KHAS BLANGS PA'I TSUL KHRIMS RNAM DAG BSRUNG NA RTOGS PA'I BSTAN PA 'DZIN PA YIN)

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:49.080
but if you keep the vows that you agreed to keep--
"Okay, I won't kill, I won't steal,

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.720
I won't hurt other people's relationships,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.360
I won't lie, and I won't use alcohol or drugs."

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:02.840
If you keep those, then you are a Dharma Master of the real teachings, of the inner teachings.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:07.200
The teachings as ideas--tokpay tenpa (RTOGS PA'I BSTAN PA),

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:11.480
dompa sum ne kyang rang re lak tu lun nge so tar yin--
(SDOM PA GSUM NAS KYANG RANG RES
LAG TU LON NGES SO THAR YIN)

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:17.680
There's three levels of vows.
Basic kindness to other people.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:23.800
Then bodhisattva vows.
"I will try to become a Buddha to help all people."

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:27.640
And then secret vows.
"I will try to do it in one lifetime."

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.840
But these vows, he says these vows
are the ones that you can practice right away.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:41.400
They're right in your pocket. Everybody has them. Everybody's supposed to keep the ten good deeds.
You have it available.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.320
Your Dharma Master equipment
is in your pocket already.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:51.120
tsultrim denpay gelong u dang den, she sok dang.
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN, ZHES SOGS DANG,)

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.600
Then in the next picture, you see a light of the world.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:03.000
I go online to find legal images that I can show you guys

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.520
and when I look at... when I type in "happy person,"

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:10.400
this guy's face keeps coming up.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:17.560
He just looks so happy to me.
I love his picture.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.880
He just looks like he's shining with light.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.920
That's what the text says here.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:37.360
Pabongka Rinpoche quotes a sutra and the sutra says:
tsultrim denpay gelong u dang den--
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN)

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.720
a person who keeps their morality,

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.160
they are shining--they are shining light.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:53.360
Christianity says to shine your light to the world. Don't hide your goodness. Let your goodness shine.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.080
It's exactly the idea here.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:04.000
Of course, whenever there's a quotation
from an ancient book, I like to go read it.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:11.680
I like to go slow through the lam rim.
I like to enjoy it as if it were fine wine.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:16.720
I like to enjoy the taste.
So, I'm going to take you to that sutra.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:21.000
And let's read the whole section of that sutra.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.200
Okay, the sutra is called tsultrim yangdakpar denpay do (TSUL KHRIMS YANG DAG PAR LDAN PA'I MDO),

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.840
you won't see this...

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.600
this is not part of this lam rim, but he quotes it,
so I went and got the quotation for you.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:38.080
And I thought you would enjoy more context.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.360
So here we go.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:44.160
The sutra is called tsultrim yangdakpar denpay do, @Shila Sanyukta Sutra,

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:50.840
which means the Sutra of the People who Keep Good Behavior.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.800
That's the name of the sutra.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.120
It's poetry. Okay, here we go.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.520
tsultrim denpay gelong u dang den,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN,)

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.600
tsultrim trim denpa drag gyur dewa tob,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA GRAGS 'GYUR BDE BA THOB,)

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:02.840
tsultrim denpa to ri droway gyu,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA MTHO RIS 'GRO BA'I RGYU,)

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.360
tsultrim sungpe nye-ngen-da tob gyur,
(TSUL KHRIMS BSRUNGS PAS
MYA NGAN 'DA' THOB 'GYUR,)

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.880
ji tar mik me suk tong mirung tar,
(JI LTAR MIG MED GZUGS MTHONG MI RUNG LTAR,)

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.080
de shin tsultrim me na chu mi tong,
(DE BZHIN TSUL KHRIMS MED NA CHOS MI MTHONG,)

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.960
ji tar kang me lam juk ga la nu,
(JI LTAR RKANG MED LAM 'JUG GA LA NUS,)

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.800
de shin tsultrim me na tar mingyur.
(DE BZHIN TSUL KHRIMS MED NA THAR MI 'GYUR,)

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.000
Very famous. Okay, here we go.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.720
tsultrim denpay gelong u dang den--

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:24.560
A person who is keeping their vows
is like a shining light for the whole world.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.160
tsultrim denpa drak gyur dewa tob--

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.840
people who keep their vows,
keep their morality,

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:36.800
they become "real" famous,
beautiful famous--

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.320
not like these famous criminals or famous politicians.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:45.840
The person who keeps their vows,
they are good famous.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.640
dewa tob--
(BDE BA THOB)

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.720
and because of that, they're always happy.
They always feel happy.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.080
tsultrim denpa to ri droway gyu--

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:58.840
If you keep your good behavior,
if you're nice to other people,

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.400
then after you die, you don't have to worry;
you're going to go to a nice place.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.720
tsultrim sungpe nye-ngen-da tob gyur--

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:10.480
And people who keep their vows,
they get to go to nirvana.
Not other people.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:14.080
ji tar mik me suk tong mi rung tar--

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:23.080
if someone took a knife and tore out your eyes, if someone tore out your eyes--

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.760
ji tar mik me suk tong--
(JI LTAR MIG MED GZUGS MTHONG)

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.760
you wouldn't be able to see anything.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.920
de shin tsultrim me na chu mi tong--

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:35.840
and the person who is not nice to other people
is blind to the Dharma.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:40.240
They will never understand the Dharma.
It's like you took their eyes out.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:48.080
A person who is not nice to other people has ruined their eyes and they cannot see the Dharma.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:54.400
They can sit in the lam rim teaching for years and years, and they will understand nothing.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.400
ji tar kang me lam juk ga la nu--

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:03.000
If someone cut your legs off,
you cannot climb to the top of Mount Everest.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:09.160
If you don't keep good behavior to other people, or be nice to other people, forget the rest of Buddhism.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.120
de shin tsultrim me na tar mingyur--

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:17.720
a person with no moral life will never go to freedom.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:24.120
gang na gelong dulwa dzinpa yupay chok der nangwa dang che--
(GANG NA DGE SLONG 'DUL BA 'DZIN PA YOD PA'I PHYOGS DER SNANG BA DANG BCAS)

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:31.920
any place in the world where
there's one person being nice to other people,

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:37.040
we can say there's light in that part of the world.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:43.560
There's not darkness.
That part of this world is free of darkness.
Spiritual darkness.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.160
u dang che--
('OD DANG BCAS)

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.040
covered with light.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.920
sa chok de nga nyi kyi ma tongpar tong--
(SA PHYOGS DE NGA NYID KYIS
MA STONGS PAR MTHONG,)

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:56.080
If there's one person being nice
to another person in this world

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:00.480
and they're standing in a house, then I am in that house.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.400
Buddha says, "Then I am in that house."

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.920
It's very beautiful. He says,

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:07.960
nga nyi kyi ma tong--
(NGA NYID KYIS MA STONGS)

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.200
"The house is not empty of me."

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:13.720
So he makes almost like a Buddhist joke,
you know? He says

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:24.480
if one person in a house
is being nice to other people in a house,
then there's no emptiness of Buddha in that house.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:28.320
It means, "I am there.
I am there."

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.680
And he's not being metaphorical.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:39.240
If you have a choice, would you like the historical Buddha to come to your house and have lunch with you?

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:43.240
Or would you rather have a person who's keeping their vows have lunch with you?

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.800
Then take the person who's keeping their vows,
because that's the real Buddha.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.840
That's the real Buddha, not the historical Buddha.
Okay? That's cool.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.000
ma tong par...
(MA STONGS PAR)

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:58.120
...sa chok der nga-ang tuk le chung ngur shuk.
(SA PHYOGS DER NGA'ANG THUGS
LAS CHUNG NGUR BZHUGS)

00:12:58.120 --> 00:12:59.520
This is very beautiful.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:09.160
He says that if a person is being nice to other people, there's light in that place. In that city there is light.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:15.560
If a person is being nice to another person,
I am in that city.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.200
I'm still there. I am in that city.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:23.440
And tuk le chung ngur gyur (@THUGS LAS CHUNG NGUR GYUR)--

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.320
you made my life easier.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:32.840
Wow! The Buddha said to us,
"Listen, I've got to take care of a lot of people,
this is stressful!"

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.040
This is like being a mom with a lot of kids.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:41.640
"I have to be everywhere in the universe.
I have to keep watching out for everybody."

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:49.040
@Quan Yin, right? It means keep listening in case someone says, "Mom, I need help!"

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.800
@Avalokiteshvara.
"Who needs help? Who needs help?"

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:59.400
And Buddha says, "You want to be nice to Buddha?"  Yeah.
"Give me a break!"

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:05.600
What's a break? It's like when
the babysitter comes over and takes Amalie

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:12.920
from Nick and Erin, and says, "You guys relax,
you guys go to Butterfly Burger.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:21.080
I'll take care of the kids. I'll watch the kids.
I'll watch Amalie," or Ava--Adam and Katie's baby.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.160
"Don't worry, I'll watch the kid."

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:29.680
So Buddha says if one person, in one place,
is being nice to another person,

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.160
I get to take a break.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:37.160
Because they're taking care of everything.
They're the babysitter now.

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:40.160
It's a very beautiful word--tuk le chung ngur--
(THUGS LAS CHUNG NGUR)

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:46.720
That place I don't have to get involved. I can take care of other places because that place is already taken care of.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.320
That's very beautiful.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:50.600
shuk sungpa sok tar kye chu--
(BZHUGS GSUNGS PA SOGS LTAR KHYAD CHOS)

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:54.960
now that's a quotation also. I went and got it for you.

00:14:55.680 --> 00:15:01.040
It's from dulwa shung dampa ('DUL BA GZHUNG DAM PA), which is called
"The Perfect Book on Morality."

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:06.280
This quotation was hard to find, and some people have not been able to find it.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:11.960
But because we have John Brady's database,
I was able to find it.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:24.840
ngay chok der nangwar drakpa dang, nangwar gyurpa dang, rabtu nangwar gyurpa dang, ngay chok der ma tongpar drakpa dang, dulwa dzinpay gangsak de tabu chok gang na nepa dey chok su deshin shekpa tuk le chungwar gyur ro--
(NGA'I PHYOGS DER SNANG BAR GRAGS PA DANG, SNANG BAR GYUR PA DANG, RAB TU SNANG BAR GYUR PA DANG, NGA'I PHYOGS DER MA STONGS PAR GRAGS PA DANG, 'DUL BA 'DZIN PA'I GANG ZAG DE LTA BU PHYOGS GANG NA GNAS PA DE'I PHYOGS SU DE BZHIN GSHEGS PA THUGS LAS CHUNG BAR 'GYUR RO,)

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.400
"I can take a break."
So the ending is the clue.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:31.080
And we found it in that text.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:37.800
rang re bu gang chen la chiy gyel kab na mepay kye chu.
(RANG RE BOD GANGS CAN LA PHYI'I RGYAL KHAB NA MED PA'I KHYAD CHOS)

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:40.640
And then he...

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:45.240
you know, old Tibet, where my teacher came from...

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:54.680
My teacher grew up in Tibet in the 1920s and the 1930s. In old Tibet, they didn't have cars.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:59.040
They didn't even have bicycles.

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:09.960
There's a story about the first aluminum pot that made it to Tibet. It became a famous thing.

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.600
So anyway, these things weren't there.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:21.400
So Pabongka Rinpoche, who's speaking,
probably in the 1920s I'm guessing,

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:31.840
he says look, we aren't like those other countries.
They have steam ships.
They have airplanes.
They have cars.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:40.560
We're just sheep herders and yak herders.
We're here in the Himalayan mountains
and we don't have any of that stuff.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:46.160
But, we got one thing here.
We got Dharma!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:51.520
They got airplanes. They got cars. They got ships.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:56.200
Okay, that's cool, but we got Dharma.
That's what we got.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:01.160
And it's trel yun pen dey gyi tsawa ('PHRAL YUN PHAN BDE'I GYI RTZA BA)--

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:06.360
it's the only thing that can really make you happy.
A car cannot make you happy. Airplane.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:11.840
It's nice to have a car.
Dharma people should have a car.
Dharma people should have airplanes.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.680
Dharma people should have ships.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.080
But it's not necessarily going to make you happy.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.280
But we got the thing here in our country,

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:23.080
we got the Dharma.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:28.920
And trel dang yun ('PHRAL DANG YUN) means
it makes you happy day to day,
and it makes you happy after you die.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.240
It takes care of you after you die.

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:34.120
sanggye kyi tenpa di yin...
(SANGS RGYAS KYI BSTAN PA 'DI YIN)

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.480
de dak mi dak ni...
(DE DAG MI DAG NI)

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.320
kangpa dang, mi mangwa dang, chu dze trawa sok min gyi.
(KHANG PA DANG, MI MANG BA DANG,
MCHOD RDZAS BKRA BA SOGS MIN GYI)

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:47.840
So how do we know the Dharma is
in good shape in a country?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.720
How do we know that the Dharma is strong in a country?

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:57.520
How how can you tell
whether or not Dharma strong in a country?

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:02.480
kangpa (KHANG PA)--
it doesn't depend on how many tall buildings
you have in your country.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.160
mi mangwa (MI MANG BA)--

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:09.640
it doesn't have anything to do with how big the population is in your country.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:17.880
chu dze trawa sok (MCHOD RDZAS BKRA BA SOGS)--
it doesn't even have to do with how beautiful you can make offerings in the temple or the churches.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.360
It's not that.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.960
tenpay tsawa so so tarpay tsultrim di nyi la rak le--
(BSTAN PA'I RTZA BA SO SO THAR PA'I
TSUL KHRIMS 'DI NYID LA RAG LAS)

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:28.840
if someone is being nice to another person,

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.000
then we can say that country is advanced,

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.040
and that country is progressed,

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.560
and that country is modern,

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.640
and that country is an important country,

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.120
and that country is a superpower.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:47.240
If a few people are trying to be nice to other people,

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:49.560
then that country is a superpower.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.480
It doesn't depend on how many rockets or bombs
you have, or things like that. Okay?

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.480
It's a very beautiful idea.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:00.400
de nyi nampar dakpa shik ma jungwar--
(DE NYID RNAM PAR DAG PA
ZHIG MA BYUNG BAR)

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:06.840
now, suppose you start
to lose the Dharma in your country.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.440
Suppose you had the Dharma,

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:14.560
or lam rim videos reached your internet in your country,

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:19.320
but rang gyu la nub (RANG RGYUD LA NUB)...

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:23.440
and we have a picture here.
This is a picture I took near my house.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:28.000
It's a sunset near my house.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:35.040
The other day was my partner's birthday, Veronica's birthday, so we took a long hike.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:40.120
It's like an hour and a half,
and you climb this tall mountain.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:48.240
And from up there, we watched the sun go down,
and it was a strange sunset.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:58.120
Usually the sun here is very bright,
but the sun started to go down, and then this black cloud started to come down on top of the sun.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.160
It was kind of strange, you know?

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:04.000
First the sun got dimmer and dimmer and dimmer.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:08.560
And these black clouds came in, and then the sun sank.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:13.040
In English, we say the sun sank.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:16.240
And everything got dark and gray.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:20.760
And we had trouble because we were enjoying dessert and we were having a picnic.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:25.000
We ran out of time and we had to run home
because it was getting dark.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.840
Why are we talking about that?

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:29.840
Pabongka Rinpoche says

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:34.040
there are places where the sun sets in your heart--

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.280
inside your chest.

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:43.800
The sun goes down, and your heart becomes dark and your chest becomes dark.

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:50.080
The sunlight goes away and the darkness
starts to come in your own heart.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:54.440
So he says something very powerful in Tibetan.
He uses the verb nub (NUB),

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:58.400
which means the "sun went down" in your heart.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:05.480
So, if you cannot be nice to other people

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:08.360
day-to-day, hour-to-hour, minute-to-minute,

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:15.200
then that Dharma went down in your heart.
The sun of the Dharma went down in your heart.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:22.680
chir jikten na tenpa sa dar do dar yin yang rang la tenpa gu nub tu gyurwa yin--
(SPYIR 'JIG RTEN NA BSTAN PA SA DAR RDO DAR YIN YANG RANG LA BSTAN PA SGOS NUB TU 'GYUR BA YIN)

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:33.200
The teachings may have spread through
the internet, and Tim Lowenhaupt's hard work,
to many, many countries.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:36.600
Maybe the Dharma has spread to many, many countries.

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:41.760
The internet has carried
the lam rim to many, many countries,

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:46.800
and Tim's one hundred-something volunteers
are translating it into many languages,

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.280
but if you're not nice to other people,

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:55.240
the Dharma died in your country.
Okay? Very, very sad.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:58.600
The sun went down in your country.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:04.800
It doesn't matter it's on the internet.
It doesn't matter it spread to your country.
It doesn't matter you are translating it.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:11.040
If the translators aren't nice to each other
then the Dharma... then the sun went down.

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:13.760
It's very sad. It's a terrible image. I don't like it.
Let's go on.

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:17.480
do ting-ngen-dzin gyi gyelpo le
(MDO TING NGE 'DZIN GYI RGYAL PO LAS)

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:26.480
This is a very, very famous sutra called @Samādhi Rāja which means the "King of Meditation Sutra."

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:36.040
It's a very famous sutra called the King of Meditation.  It's a very beautiful sutra and it actually is like the beginning of a meditation manual.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:54.160
Okay, suppose someone for billions of years,

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:59.160
equal to the grains of sand in the Ganges River...

00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:05.240
The Ganges River is... sometimes it can take an hour to cross the Ganges River on a bridge; it's huge.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:14.200
So imagine all the drops of water, or imagine all the grains of sand in the Ganges River.

00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:21.560
Each one is a billion years.
Each grain of sand is a billion years.

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:28.800
Okay, and for that many billion years, out of great faith, you offer to the Buddha

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:32.280
a beautiful dinner, or

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:36.800
delicious drinks to drink, or

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:39.040
religious umbrellas,

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:41.160
sun cover,

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:44.600
or these spiritual flags that we fly,

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:48.280
or you offer these butter lamps,

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:51.240
for billions of years.

00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:53.600
And not to one Buddha--

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:58.240
to tens of millions of Buddhas.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:02.080
And you make these offerings for billions of years.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:08.160
gang gi dam chu rabtu jikpa dang, der shek tenpa gakpar gyurway tse--
@GANG GIS DAM CHOS RAB TU 'JIG PA DANG,
BDER GSHEGS BSTAN PA 'GAG PAR 'GYUR BA'I TSE

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:13.560
and the other hand--this is very, very beautiful--
when things get hard,

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:20.760
when things in the world get hard, when there's a problem in the world, when there's a virus,

00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:28.080
when there's not a lot of money,
and there's not a lot of food.
In our country, there's not a lot toilet paper.

00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:31.000
When things get hard, that's very beautiful.

00:24:31.840 --> 00:24:34.120
gang gi dam chu ratbu jikpa--
(GANG GIS DAM CHOS RAB TU 'JIG PA)

00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:40.080
when people are forgetting
about being nice to each other,
and when people are afraid,

00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:45.480
and people are holding on to their money,
and people are holding on to their food,
they are not sharing with other people,

00:24:45.960 --> 00:24:48.680
der shek tenpa gakpar gyur--
(BDER GSHEGS BSTAN PA 'GAG PAR 'GYUR)

00:24:49.440 --> 00:24:55.760
at that moment, the Dharma is dying in those countries because people are not being nice to each other.

00:24:56.160 --> 00:24:59.160
nyin tsen du ni lappa chik chupa--
(NYIN MTSAN DU NI BSLAB PA GCIG SPYOD PA)

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:08.200
but if there's one person
in those dangerous times, dark times, virus times...

00:25:08.200 --> 00:25:12.760
if there's one person being nice to another person,

00:25:12.760 --> 00:25:15.160
sunam di ni dewe che drak chak--
(BSOD NAMS 'DI NI DE BAS BYE BRAG 'PHAGS,)

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:23.480
the good seeds, the good karma,
done by a person during dark days

00:25:23.480 --> 00:25:30.920
is more valuable than the person who gives billions of offerings to the Buddha when things are going well.

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:37.240
So a person who is nice to one other person

00:25:37.600 --> 00:25:45.040
during the virus days, a person who is generous to one other person during difficult times,

00:25:46.240 --> 00:25:53.520
that's more karma
than a billion people offering veggie burgers

00:25:53.960 --> 00:25:57.120
to a billion Buddhas for a billion years.

00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.160
I'll say it again. It's hard to say.

00:26:00.320 --> 00:26:06.120
If one person during the virus times
when things are difficult,

00:26:06.960 --> 00:26:11.960
is nice to another person,
that good karma is more powerful

00:26:12.320 --> 00:26:18.600
than offering things to a billion lamas for a billion years

00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:22.800
when things are easy, when times are easy.

00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:28.760
So I think those of us
who are studying lam rim right now,

00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:32.600
we're in such a lucky place.
There's a lot of fear.

00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:39.040
These are dark times and
there is a lot of fear and a lot of worry, and

00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:43.800
if we do one small good thing during this time,

00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:49.920
it's more powerful than people doing nice things
for hundreds of years when it's easy.

00:26:49.920 --> 00:26:53.080
All right, so we're lucky to have such a difficult time.

00:26:53.080 --> 00:27:02.960
I went and found the quotation and it's exactly correct. It's exactly quoted correctly.

00:27:03.120 --> 00:27:06.000
shepa tar nyin tsen du druk tu du sum gyi sanggye la...
(ZHES PA LTAR NYIN MTSAN DUS DRUG TU DUS GSUM GYI SANGS RGYAS LA)

00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:09.360
chupa pulwa le nyik dundir tsultrim sungwa pen yon che--
(MCHOD PA PHUL BA LAS SNYIGS DUS 'DIR TSUL KHRIMS BSRUNG BA PHAN YON CHE)

00:27:10.160 --> 00:27:13.840
you could, day and night,

00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:18.680
he says du druk tu du sum (DUS DRUG TU DUS GSUM)...

00:27:18.680 --> 00:27:22.720
du sum (DUS GSUM) means Buddhas of the past, present, and future.

00:27:22.720 --> 00:27:27.520
It means any person who got enlightened before,

00:27:28.200 --> 00:27:31.040
and any person who got enlightened today,

00:27:31.680 --> 00:27:35.080
and any person who will
ever be enlightened in the future--

00:27:35.560 --> 00:27:38.800
that's the du sum--"three times".

00:27:39.080 --> 00:27:43.800
du druk (DUS DRUG) means "six times" a day you stop and you make offerings to them,

00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:46.360
every single Buddha in history.

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:51.320
Including future history.
You stop and make offerings to them--

00:27:51.960 --> 00:27:53.480
on the one hand.

00:27:53.920 --> 00:28:03.360
On the other hand, you are in a world situation which is dangerous and frightening, and hard for everybody,

00:28:03.600 --> 00:28:10.080
and you show one kindness to another person,
your good karma is more than the other person.

00:28:10.080 --> 00:28:11.040
Okay?

00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:14.160
Those who made offerings to all the Buddhas in history.

00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:22.440
To do one nice thing to another person
during the time of the virus,
your good karma is more powerful.

00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:30.400
So I think it's amazing.
It's very good for our times, for these times.

00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:34.400
So that's a Sunlight in the Time of the Virus.

00:28:35.600 --> 00:28:38.600
Love in the Time of the Virus.
This is the time.

00:28:38.960 --> 00:28:47.000
And the karmas, all those karmas,
are millions of times more powerful during these times.

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:51.400
So take some time, relax.

00:28:51.400 --> 00:28:54.960
You can be scared.
You should be scared. It's a hard thing.

00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:59.080
You should be worried and you should be concerned.

00:28:59.720 --> 00:29:06.000
But pause from time to time and do something really nice for another person.

00:29:06.080 --> 00:29:11.920
Sacrifice something,
money or food or your time,

00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:18.840
and give it to somebody else. In this time.
And then you're a real Dharma Master.

00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:22.680
Alright. See you in the next episode.

